"""
Reads the Petclinic data, public data about medicines, food safety and prices from services of the EU and of
Belgium, and the names, classification and sightings of species from GBIF. The fields owners, owner, pets, vets
and petTypes mirror what the web pages show.
An id identifies an object within its type, so an owner and a pet can have the same id.
"""
type Query {
	"""
	Owners whose first and last name start with the given texts, one page at a time.
	The names match in upper or lower case.
	A page past the last one holds an empty list of owners.
	"""
	owners(
		"The start of the first name. Leave it out, or pass an empty text, to match any first name."
		firstName: String = ""
		"The start of the last name. Leave it out, or pass an empty text, to match any last name."
		lastName: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of owners on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): OwnerPage!

	"One owner with their pets and visits, or null when owner not found for the provided id."
	owner(id: ID!): Owner

	"""
	Pets whose name starts with the given text and whose type has the given name, one page at a time.
	The name and the type match in upper or lower case.
	A page past the last one holds an empty list of pets.
	"""
	pets(
		"The start of the pet's name. Leave it out, or pass an empty text, to match any name."
		name: String = ""
		"The name of a pet type as the petTypes query lists it, for example cat. Leave it out, or pass an empty text, to match any type."
		type: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of pets on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): PetPage!

	"Every veterinarian of the clinic."
	vets: [Vet!]!

	"The kinds of pet the clinic treats, sorted by name."
	petTypes: [PetType!]!

	# The fields below read public services of the EU and of Belgium. Each name starts with the
	# service it reads: ema, rasff, famhp or eurostat.

	# The European Medicines Agency (EMA) publishes each table of its website as one report,
	# refreshed twice a day. Each ema field reads one report.

	"""
	Medicines that the European Medicines Agency (EMA) has evaluated for the EU market, for humans and for animals,
	one page at a time.
	The report holds about 2,700 medicines, and a medicine with every field is about 500 tokens. Narrow the list
	with search, category, status or species, and select only the fields the question needs. To count medicines,
	select only totalMedicines.
	"""
	emaMedicines(
		"Text that the name, a common name, an active substance or a therapeutic area of the medicine contains, in upper or lower case, for example amoxicillin. Leave it out to match every medicine."
		search: String = ""
		"Only medicines for humans, or only medicines for animals. Leave it out for both."
		category: EmaCategory
		"Only medicines with this status, in upper or lower case, for example Authorised. Leave it out for every status."
		status: String = ""
		"Text that one of the target species of a veterinary medicine contains, for example Dogs. Few veterinary medicines name their species in EMA's data, so this filter misses many of them."
		species: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of medicines on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaMedicinePage!

	"""
	The documents of the European public assessment reports (EPAR) of EMA's medicines, such as assessment reports
	and product information, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 20,000 documents, and a document with every field is about 130 tokens. Narrow the list
	with search, productNumber or type, and select only the fields the question needs. To count documents, select
	only totalDocuments.
	"""
	emaEparDocuments(
		"Text that the title, the medicine name or the reference number of the document contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every document."
		search: String = ""
		"Only the documents of the medicine with this product number, as emaMedicines returns it, for example EMEA/H/C/000619."
		productNumber: String = ""
		"Only documents of this type, for example assessment-report or product-information."
		type: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of documents on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaDocumentPage!

	"""
	The other documents of the EMA website, such as press releases, guidelines, meeting minutes and agendas,
	one page at a time.
	The report holds about 50,000 documents, and a document with every field is about 120 tokens. Narrow the list
	with search or type, and select only the fields the question needs. To count documents, select only
	totalDocuments.
	"""
	emaDocuments(
		"Text that the title or the reference number of the document contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every document."
		search: String = ""
		"Only documents of this type, for example press-release or minutes."
		type: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of documents on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaDocumentPage!

	"""
	The events that EMA organises or takes part in, past and planned, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 2,500 events, and an event with every field is about 110 tokens. Narrow the list with
	search, and select only the fields the question needs. To count events, select only totalEvents.
	"""
	emaEvents(
		"Text that the title or the location of the event contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every event."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of events on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaEventPage!

	"""
	The general pages of the EMA website, such as guidance on procedures, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 1,100 website pages, and a website page with every field is about 120 tokens. Narrow the
	list with search, and select only the fields the question needs. To count website pages, select only
	totalArticles.
	"""
	emaWebsiteArticles(
		"Text that the title or the summary of the page contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every page."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of website pages on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaWebsiteArticlePage!

	"EMA's opinions on medicines meant for use outside the EU, under the EU-M4all procedure, one page at a time."
	emaOutsideEuOpinions(
		"Text that the name, an active substance, a common name or a therapeutic area of the medicine contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every opinion."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of opinions on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaOutsideEuOpinionPage!

	"The herbal substances that EMA has assessed or plans to assess, one page at a time."
	emaHerbalSubstances(
		"Text that the Latin, English or botanical name of the substance contains, in upper or lower case, for example valerian. Leave it out to match every substance."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of substances on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaHerbalSubstancePage!

	"""
	EMA's assessments of the maximum residue limits of substances used in veterinary medicines: how much may remain
	in food from treated animals. One page at a time.
	"""
	emaMaximumResidueLimits(
		"Text that the title or the active substance contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every assessment."
		search: String = ""
		"Text that one of the target species contains, for example Bovine. Leave it out for every species."
		species: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of assessments on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaMaximumResidueLimitPage!

	"""
	The orphan designations for medicines that treat rare diseases, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 3,300 designations, and a designation with every field is about 120 tokens. Narrow the
	list with search or status, and select only the fields the question needs. To count designations, select only
	totalDesignations.
	"""
	emaOrphanDesignations(
		"Text that a medicine name, an active substance or the intended use contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every designation."
		search: String = ""
		"Only designations with this status, in upper or lower case: Positive, Withdrawn, Expired or Negative. Leave it out for every status."
		status: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of designations on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaOrphanDesignationPage!

	"""
	EMA's decisions on paediatric investigation plans, the studies of medicines in children, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 3,400 decisions, and a decision with every field is about 250 tokens. Narrow the list
	with search, and select only the fields the question needs. To count decisions, select only totalPlans.
	"""
	emaPaediatricInvestigationPlans(
		"Text that an active substance, an invented name or a condition contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every decision."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of decisions on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaPaediatricInvestigationPlanPage!

	"""
	EMA's single assessments of periodic safety update reports (PSUSA), one page at a time.
	The report holds about 2,700 assessments, and an assessment with every field is about 110 tokens. Narrow the
	list with search, and select only the fields the question needs. To count assessments, select only
	totalAssessments.
	"""
	emaPeriodicSafetyAssessments(
		"Text that an active substance or the procedure number contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every assessment."
		search: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of assessments on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaPeriodicSafetyAssessmentPage!

	"The procedures that change authorised medicines, with EMA's opinions on them, one page at a time."
	emaPostAuthorisationProcedures(
		"Text that the name, an active substance or a common name of the medicine contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every procedure."
		search: String = ""
		"Only procedures on medicines for humans, or only on medicines for animals. Leave it out for both."
		category: EmaCategory
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of procedures on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaPostAuthorisationProcedurePage!

	"""
	EMA's news items and press releases, one page at a time.
	The report holds about 3,900 news items, and a news item with every field is about 120 tokens. Narrow the list
	with search or topic, and select only the fields the question needs. To count news items, select only totalNews.
	"""
	emaNews(
		"Text that the title, the summary or a related medicine contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every news item."
		search: String = ""
		"Text that one of the topics contains, for example Pharmacovigilance. Leave it out for every topic."
		topic: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of news items on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaNewsItemPage!

	"The referrals, EU-wide reviews of the safety or benefit of medicines, one page at a time."
	emaReferrals(
		"Text that the name, a common name or a medicine of the referral contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every referral."
		search: String = ""
		"Only referrals about medicines for humans, or only about medicines for animals. Leave it out for both."
		category: EmaCategory
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of referrals on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaReferralPage!

	"The shortages of medicines in the EU that EMA monitors, one page at a time."
	emaShortages(
		"Text that the medicine or a common name contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every shortage."
		search: String = ""
		"Only shortages with this status, in upper or lower case: Shortage ongoing, Shortage resolved or Medicine discontinued. Leave it out for every status."
		status: String = ""
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of shortages on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaShortagePage!

	"""
	The direct healthcare professional communications (DHPC): letters that tell doctors, pharmacists and veterinarians
	about new safety issues of medicines. One page at a time.
	"""
	emaSafetyCommunications(
		"Text that the medicine, an active substance or another medicine of the communication contains, in upper or lower case. Leave it out to match every communication."
		search: String = ""
		"Only communications about medicines for humans, or only about medicines for animals. Leave it out for both."
		category: EmaCategory
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of communications on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): EmaSafetyCommunicationPage!

	# RASFF Window publishes the notifications of the EU's Rapid Alert System for Food and Feed.

	"""
	Notifications of the EU's Rapid Alert System for Food and Feed (RASFF) about risks found in food, feed and
	pet food, one page at a time, the most recently validated first. For the notifications about pet food, filter on
	the id of the product category pet food, which rasffProductCategories lists.
	RASFF holds about 33,000 notifications, and a notification with every field is about 130 tokens. Narrow the
	list with the filter, and select only the fields the question needs. To count notifications, select only
	totalNotifications.
	"""
	rasffNotifications(
		"The filters. Leave it out for every notification."
		filter: RasffNotificationFilter = {}
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"The number of notifications on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit."
		size: Int! = 10
	): RasffNotificationPage!

	"One RASFF notification with its details, or null when RASFF does not publish a notification with this id."
	rasffNotification(
		"The id of the notification, as rasffNotifications returns it."
		id: ID!
	): RasffNotification

	"The product categories of RASFF notifications, such as pet food, sorted by description."
	rasffProductCategories: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The product types of RASFF notifications, such as food and feed, sorted by description."
	rasffProductTypes: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The hazard categories of RASFF notifications, such as foreign bodies or pathogenic micro-organisms, sorted by description."
	rasffHazardCategories: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The risk decisions of RASFF notifications, such as serious or not serious, sorted by description."
	rasffRiskDecisions: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The classifications of RASFF notifications, such as alert notification or border rejection notification, sorted by description."
	rasffNotificationClassifications: [RasffTerm!]!

	"What can lead to a RASFF notification, such as a consumer complaint or a border control, sorted by description."
	rasffNotificationBases: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The measures that authorities take about a product, such as a recall from consumers, sorted by description."
	rasffActionsTaken: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The statuses of RASFF notifications, sorted by description."
	rasffNotificationStatuses: [RasffTerm!]!

	"The countries that RASFF notifications name as the origin or a destination of a product, sorted by name."
	rasffCountries: [RasffCountry!]!

	"The members of the RASFF network, which send the notifications, sorted by name."
	rasffNetworkMembers: [RasffMember!]!

	# The medicines database of the Belgian Federal Agency for Medicines and Health Products
	# (FAMHP) publishes its reference data.

	"""
	The animal species that veterinary medicines can be authorised for in Belgium, sorted by name,
	from the medicines database of the Belgian Federal Agency for Medicines and Health Products (FAMHP).
	The list holds about 280 species, about 9,000 tokens with every field. Narrow it with name, and select only the
	fields the question needs.
	"""
	famhpTargetSpecies(
		"Text that the name of the species contains, in upper or lower case, for example dog. Leave it out for every species."
		name: String = ""
	): [FamhpTargetSpecies!]!

	"The types of authorisation of medicines in Belgium, sorted by name, from the FAMHP medicines database."
	famhpAuthorisationTypes: [FamhpAuthorisationType!]!

	"The legal bases of applications for medicines in Belgium, sorted by name, from the FAMHP medicines database."
	famhpLegalBases(
		"Only the legal bases for medicines for humans, or only for medicines for animals. Leave it out for both."
		usage: FamhpUsage
	): [FamhpLegalBasis!]!

	"How medicines may be supplied in Belgium, for example on medical prescription, sorted by name, from the FAMHP medicines database."
	famhpDeliveryModes: [FamhpDeliveryMode!]!

	"The types of documents that the FAMHP medicines database holds for a medicine, such as the leaflet, in the database's own order."
	famhpDocumentTypes: [FamhpDocumentType!]!

	# Eurostat publishes the EU's harmonised index of consumer prices (HICP), which has
	# categories for pets, pet products and veterinary services.

	"Describes how a monthly consumer price index has change for pets and pet products in a country, with 2025 as 100, from Eurostat."
	eurostatPetPriceIndex(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"How much the prices of a pet category in a country changed from the month before, in percent, month by month, from Eurostat."
	eurostatPetPriceMonthlyChange(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"""
	How much the prices of a pet category in a country changed from the same month a year before, in percent,
	month by month, from Eurostat. This is the inflation rate of the category.
	"""
	eurostatPetPriceAnnualChange(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"""
	How much the average prices of a pet category in a country over the latest 12 months changed from the average of the
	12 months before, in percent, month by month, from Eurostat.
	"""
	eurostatPetPriceMovingAverageChange(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"""
	The monthly price index of a pet category in a country as it would be if tax rates had stayed the same, with 2025
	as 100, from Eurostat. Its difference from eurostatPetPriceIndex shows the effect of changes in taxes.
	"""
	eurostatPetPriceIndexAtConstantTaxRates(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"How many percentage points a pet category contributed to the annual inflation of the euro area, month by month, from Eurostat."
	eurostatPetPriceContributionToEuroAreaInflation(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The first month, written YYYY-MM. Leave out from and to for the latest 12 months."
		from: String
		"The last month, written YYYY-MM. Leave it out to end with the latest month."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"The yearly average of the price index of a pet category in a country, from Eurostat. The unit of the series names the base year."
	eurostatPetPriceAnnualAverageIndex(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first year, written YYYY. Leave out from and to for the latest 5 years."
		from: String
		"The last year, written YYYY. Leave it out to end with the latest year."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"How much the yearly average prices of a pet category in a country changed from the year before, in percent, from Eurostat."
	eurostatPetPriceAnnualAverageChange(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first year, written YYYY. Leave out from and to for the latest 5 years."
		from: String
		"The last year, written YYYY. Leave it out to end with the latest year."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	"""
	The share of household spending that goes to a pet category in a country, in parts per thousand, year by year,
	from Eurostat. Eurostat uses it to weight the category in the price index.
	"""
	eurostatPetSpendingWeight(
		"The pet category."
		category: EurostatPetCategory! = PETS_AND_PET_PRODUCTS
		"The Eurostat code of the country, for example BE for Belgium, or of a group, for example EU27_2020 for the European Union."
		country: String! = "BE"
		"The first year, written YYYY. Leave out from and to for the latest 5 years."
		from: String
		"The last year, written YYYY. Leave it out to end with the latest year."
		to: String
	): EurostatSeries!

	# GBIF, the Global Biodiversity Information Facility, publishes data about where species live.
	# The fields below are generated from GBIF's OpenAPI documents, one field for each read
	# operation. These first ones read the names and the classification of species.

	"""
	Splits a scientific name into its parts, such as the genus, the specific epithet and the authorship.
	Parse a scientific name.
	Parses a scientific name string and returns the ParsedName version of it.
	Accepts multiple parameters each with a single name. Make sure you URL encode the names properly.
	"""
	gbifParseName(
		"A scientific name to parse. Repeat to parse several names"
		name: [String!]
	): [GbifParsedName]

	"""
	Lists the names of species and other taxa, by checklist or by exact name.
	List all name usages.
	Lists all name usages across all checklists.
	"""
	gbifNameUsages(
		"A UUID of a checklist dataset."
		datasetKey: [ID!]
		"Filters by the source identifier."
		sourceId: String
		"A name without authorship, to match exactly."
		name: String
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"""
		The number of results on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit.
		"""
		size: Int! = 10
	): GbifNameUsagePage

	"""
	One name usage by its key: a scientific name as one checklist uses it, with its rank, its taxonomic status and
	its classification. In the GBIF backbone taxonomy, 5219173 is Canis lupus and 6164210 is Canis lupus familiaris,
	the dog.
	"""
	gbifNameUsage(
		"""
		The key of the name usage, as gbifSearchNames or gbifSpeciesMatch returns it, for example 5219173 for Canis
		lupus or 6164210 for Canis lupus familiaris, the dog, in the GBIF backbone taxonomy.
		"""
		usageKey: Int!
	): GbifNameUsage

	"""
	The common names of a species or another taxon in many languages, by the key of the species.
	Name usage vernacular names by id.
	Retrieves all vernacular names for a name usage.
	"""
	gbifNameUsageVernacularNames(
		"""
		The key of the name usage, as gbifSearchNames or gbifSpeciesMatch returns it, for example 5219173 for Canis
		lupus or 6164210 for Canis lupus familiaris, the dog, in the GBIF backbone taxonomy.
		"""
		usageKey: Int!
