	"""
	Finds the GBIF key of a species, or of another taxon, from its scientific name, for example Canis lupus
	familiaris for the dog or Felis catus for the cat. Most other gbif fields take the key it returns as usageKey or
	taxonKey.
	Fuzzy name match service (Version 2).
	Fuzzy matches scientific names against the Taxonomy with the optional classification provided. If a
	classification is provided and strict is not set to true, the default matching will also try to match against
	these if no direct match is found for the name parameter alone.
	Additionally, a lookup may be performed by providing the usageKey which will short-circuit the name-based
	matching and ONLY use the given key, either finding the concept or returning no match.
	"""
	gbifSpeciesMatch(
		"""
		The key of the name usage, as gbifSearchNames or gbifSpeciesMatch returns it, for example 5219173 for Canis
		lupus or 6164210 for Canis lupus familiaris, the dog, in the GBIF backbone taxonomy.
		"""
		usageKey: String
		"""
		The taxonID to match. Matches to a taxonID will take precedence over scientificName values supplied. A
		comparison of the matched scientific and taxonID is performed to check for inconsistencies. See Darwin core term
		taxonID for more details. Sources of recognised identifiers include: International Plant Names Index (IPNI) -
		Example identifiers:urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:2006-1ipni:2006-1https://www.ipni.org/n/2006-1World Register of
		Marine Species - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:105838AphiaID:105838Dyntaxa. Svensk
		taxonomisk databas - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:dyntaxa.se:Taxon:103038The Integrated Taxonomic Information
		System - Example identifiers:itis:179628tsn:179628United Kingdom Species Inventory (UKSI) - Example
		identifiers:NHMSYS0000530537
		"""
		taxonID: String
		"""
		The taxonConceptID to match. Matches to a taxonConceptID will take precedence over scientificName values
		supplied. A comparison of the matched scientific and taxonConceptID is performed to check for inconsistencies.
		See Darwin core term taxonConceptID for more details. Sources of recognised identifiers include: International
		Plant Names Index (IPNI) - Example
		identifiers:urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:2006-1ipni:2006-1https://www.ipni.org/n/2006-1World Register of Marine
		Species - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:105838AphiaID:105838Dyntaxa. Svensk taxonomisk
		databas - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:dyntaxa.se:Taxon:103038The Integrated Taxonomic Information System -
		Example identifiers:itis:179628tsn:179628United Kingdom Species Inventory (UKSI) - Example
		identifiers:NHMSYS0000530537
		"""
		taxonConceptID: String
		"""
		The scientificNameID to match. Matches to a scientificNameID will take precedence over scientificName values
		supplied. A comparison of the matched scientific and scientificNameID is performed to check for inconsistencies.
		See Darwin core term scientificNameID for more details Sources of recognised identifiers include: International
		Plant Names Index (IPNI) - Example
		identifiers:urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:2006-1ipni:2006-1https://www.ipni.org/n/2006-1World Register of Marine
		Species - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:marinespecies.org:taxname:105838AphiaID:105838Dyntaxa. Svensk taxonomisk
		databas - Example identifiers:urn:lsid:dyntaxa.se:Taxon:103038The Integrated Taxonomic Information System -
		Example identifiers:itis:179628tsn:179628United Kingdom Species Inventory (UKSI) - Example
		identifiers:NHMSYS0000530537
		"""
		scientificNameID: String
		"""
		The scientific name to fuzzy match against. May include the authorship and year. See Darwin core term
		scientificName for more details
		"""
		scientificName: String
		"""
		The scientific name authorship to match against. See Darwin core term scientificNameAuthorship for more details
		"""
		scientificNameAuthorship: String
		"Filters by taxonomic rank. See Darwin core term taxonRank for more details"
		taxonRank: GbifTaxonRank
		"Filters by taxonomic rank. See Darwin core term verbatimTaxonRank for more details"
		verbatimTaxonRank: String
		"""
		Generic part of the name to match when given as atomised parts instead of the full name parameter.See Darwin
		core term genericName for more details
		"""
		genericName: String
		"Specific epithet to match. See Darwin core term specificEpithet for more details"
		specificEpithet: String
		"Infraspecific epithet to match. See Darwin core term infraspecificEpithet for more details"
		infraspecificEpithet: String
		"Kingdom to match. See Darwin core term kingdom for more details"
		kingdom: String
		"Phylum to match. See Darwin core term phylum for more details"
		phylum: String
		"Order to match. See Darwin core term order for more details"
		order: String
		"Superfamily to match. See Darwin core term superfamily for more details"
		superfamily: String
		"Family to match. See Darwin core term family for more details"
		family: String
		"Subfamily to match. See Darwin core term subfamily for more details"
		subfamily: String
		"Tribe to match. See Darwin core term tribe for more details"
		tribe: String
		"Subtribe to match. See Darwin core term subtribe for more details"
		subtribe: String
		"Genus to match. See Darwin core term genus for more details"
		genus: String
		"Subgenus to match. See Darwin core term subgenus for more details"
		subgenus: String
		"Species to match. See Darwin core term species for more details"
		species: String
		"An array of usage keys to exclude from the match."
		exclude: String
		"If set to true, fuzzy matches only the given name, but never a taxon in the upper classification."
		strict: Boolean
		"If set to true, it shows alternative matches which were considered but then rejected."
		verbose: Boolean
		"The dataset key of the checklist to match against."
		checklistKey: ID
		"Class to match. See Darwin core term class for more details"
		class: String
	): GbifNameUsageMatch

